@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & your data";
    var storesSnapshots = (bool)(ViewData["StoresSnapshots"] ?? false);
    var email = ViewData["StoreEmail"];
}
<article style="max-width:70ch;">
<h1>Privacy and your data</h1>
<p class="muted">Your prescription is health data, and we treat it that way.</p>

<h2>Your photograph never leaves your device</h2>
<p>The face detection behind the virtual try-on runs entirely inside your own web
browser. The model and its runtime are served from this website — no third party
is contacted, and no photograph or camera frame is ever uploaded while you are
trying frames on.</p>

@if (storesSnapshots)
{
    <p>This shop is currently set to <strong>keep</strong> try-on snapshots you
    explicitly choose to save, so an optician can refer to them. You can still
    download an image without saving it to your file.</p>
}
else
{
    <p>This shop is currently set <strong>not to keep</strong> try-on images at
    all. The save option is switched off and the server refuses such uploads
    outright. You can still download your own picture.</p>
}

<h2>Your patient file</h2>
<p>Ordering prescription lenses creates a patient file with a reference number.
We need it to make your lenses, to remake them if something is wrong, and to
answer questions about a past order. Guests get one too, for the same reasons.</p>

<h2>Prescriptions are never overwritten</h2>
<p>When you give us a new prescription we store it as a new version. The old one
stays on file, and every order keeps its own copy of the prescription it was
dispensed against, so an invoice from years ago still reads correctly.</p>

<h2>Who can see it</h2>
<p>Our staff and opticians can see your file in order to dispense and follow up
your order. Every change to a patient record, a price or an order is recorded
with who made it and when. Clinical values are deliberately kept out of that
record, because it is read more widely than the file it describes.</p>

<h2>Correcting or deleting your data</h2>
<p>You can ask us to correct anything in your file, or to erase it. Email
<a href="mailto:@email">@email</a> and we will confirm what we hold, action the
request, and tell you what we are legally required to keep — dispensing records
generally must be retained for a period even after a request to erase.</p>
</article>
